{
  "_comment": "Records are the passport's subjects — one product, one origin story. This file IS the passport data: no chain, no dashboard, no API key. `photo` is the documentary image used on the page (hands, cloth, looms); `image` is the record sheet drawn by `npm run record:svg`, used on the passport and for print.  Prose fields (description, subtitle, attribute values) are ENGLISH: the interface speaks English, and the craft's own words (ikat, tenun, mengkudu) are the ones that stay untranslated. The 'Journey step' attribute value must equal a step label in lib/copy.ts (Seed, Loom, Trace, Teach, Regenerate, Hub, Flourish), because JourneyRail matches on it to mark the active step. PHOTO CAVEAT: photos in public/imagery/ come from the design system uploads and include AI-generated reference images — replace them with licensed community photography before publication (brief §6). Never invent figures: leave a field out rather than guessing it.  Data sourced from the Pungkas / List Tenun exhibition spreadsheet (27 handwoven cloths across 6 installation locations).  Weaver name defaults to Mama Ina Dida until real names are recorded.",
